        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 71-year-old female patient, admitted on 02/02/2022 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemia, chest X-ray, and pulse oximetry monitoring. Spirometry confirmed severely reduced airflow. She was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout the stay. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. She was discharged on 03/02/2022 in stable condition. Please continue maintenance bronchodilator therapy and arrange pulmonary follow-up. Patient education regarding exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
